raw_response:
The schema evidences these distinct entity types: an event/action, up to four involved actors, a fatality effect, a specific event location, four enclosing geographic levels, and a coordinate point.

The event is identified by event_id_cnty and maps to bsm:Action. Each actor field is independently mapped to bsm:Actor because the field names explicitly say “actor”; associated actors are separate entities rather than actor-name literals. The fatality count supports a bsm:ActionEffect linked through bsm:hasResult. The location hierarchy is modeled with bsm:Location and bsm:partOf, while latitude and longitude identify a bsm:AbsolutePoint linked through bsm:hasGeometry.

event_date is not mapped to bsm:eventStartDateTime because the column supplies only a date and does not say whether it is the action’s start rather than another event date. disorder_type, event_type, and sub_event_type are not mapped to bsm:classificationCode because their names and values are type labels, while the ontology property specifically requires a classification code. source is also not mapped to bsm:sourceIdentifier: “Baltic Monitoring Desk” names a reporting source rather than an identifier.

All IRI transformations were checked against their referenced subjects: actor_{actor1}, actor_{assoc_actor_1}, actor_{actor2}, actor_{assoc_actor_2}, effect_{event_id_cnty}_fatalities, place_{iso}_{admin1}_{admin2}_{location}, admin2_{iso}_{admin1}_{admin2}, admin1_{iso}_{admin1}, country_{iso}, region_{region}, and point_{latitude}_{longitude} are character-for-character identical at both ends. No unused transformation keys are included.

